<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36966" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōmōna</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		pomum. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The goddess of fruit and fruit-trees</i>, <i>Pomona</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 45</span></i>
			Müll.; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14, 623</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Serv. Verg. A. 7, 190</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Arn. 3, p.
			118</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>fruit-trees</i>,
				<i>fruit</i> (post-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 23</span></i>
			prooem. 1, § 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">1: Thyle larga et diutina Pomona copiosa est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 22 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> ‡
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōmōnal</span></b> , ālis,
				n., <i>the temple of Pomona</i>, <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				250</span></i> Müll.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pōmōnālis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pomona</i>, <i>Pomonal</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flamen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 45</span></i>
			 Müll.; cf. Fest. s. v. maximae dignationis, pp. 154
			and 155 Müll.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
